{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Elohim you shall not curse.</b> Even though you may think the judge has perverted your judgment, do not curse him — for no person sees his own liability." "<b>And a prince among your people you shall not curse.</b> For indeed, cursing the king and his harm falls upon the multitude as the cause of great evil and public harm, as it says: יְרָא אֶת ה' בְּנִי וָמֶלֶךְ, וְעִם שׁוֹנִים אַל תִּתְעָרָב (Proverbs 24:21)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:51.268102550Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}